    <bpmn:process id="W_W1423" name="W1423. DC-to-DC Inter-DC Inventory Rebalancing Transfer Execution &amp; In-Transit Monitoring" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Supply planning detects DC inventory imbalance; or emergency replenishment request from a DC facing stockout risk; or post-season regional rebalancing
Frequency: ~30–40 inter-DC transfers/month; higher during seasonal transitions and post-typhoon recovery
Volume: ~30–40 transfer orders/month averaging 5–20 lines per transfer (per W22); total ~150–800 transfer lines/month
Owner: Supply Planning Manager
Participants: Supply Planning Manager, Shipping DC Supervisor, Receiving DC Supervisor, Logistics Coordinator, Inventory Analyst
Source: workflow W1423 — DC-to-DC Inter-DC Inventory Rebalancing Transfer Execution &amp; In-Transit Monitoring</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1423_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1423_Lane1" name="Supply Planning Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1423_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1423_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1423_Lane2" name="Shipping DC Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1423_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1423_Lane3" name="Inventory Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1423_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1423_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1423_Lane4" name="Receiving DC Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1423_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1423_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1423_Start6" name="Supply planning detects DC inventory imbalance; or emergency replenishment request from a…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1423_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1423_Task7" name="Transfer initiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Transfer initiation: Supply Planning Manager identifies rebalancing need: (a) system generates inter-DC transfer recommendation: (i) identify SKUs where one DC has excess stock (above max level) and another DC has deficit (below safety stock), (ii) calculate optimal transfer quantity: minimum of source DC excess and destination DC deficit, (b) Supply Planning Manager reviews recommendations: (i) validate demand signal (is the deficit real or a data timing issue?), (ii) consider transit time — for inter-island transfers with 5–7 day transit, the destination DC may be replenished by vendors before the transfer arrives, (c) approve transfer orders: ~30–40/month
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–3 hours/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1423_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1423_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1423_Task8" name="Shipping DC execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Shipping DC execution: (a) Shipping DC Supervisor receives transfer order in WMS: pick items from storage locations per W106 procedures, (b) pack and stage for inter-DC transport: (i) for land transfers (Calamba–Clark): load onto company or third-party truck, (ii) for inter-island transfers (Davao–Cebu, Cebu–Calamba): stage for coastwise vessel or RORO ferry, (c) ship confirmation: system posts goods issue — inventory reduces at shipping DC, in-transit inventory increases (Dr. Inventory In-Transit / Cr. Inventory at Shipping DC)
Responsible (R): Shipping DC Supervisor / Pick Staff
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 4–8 hours/transfer</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1423_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1423_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1423_Task9" name="In-transit monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: In-transit monitoring: (a) system tracks in-transit inventory: items shipped from one DC but not yet received at another, (b) Inventory Analyst monitors daily: (i) expected arrival date vs. actual progress (vessel tracking for inter-island), (ii) flag delays: transfers in transit &gt; expected transit time + 2 days, (c) for delayed transfers: coordinate with logistics provider per W66 (inter-island logistics) to determine cause and revised ETA
Responsible (R): Inventory Analyst / Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1423_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1423_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1423_Task10" name="Receiving DC execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Receiving DC execution: (a) Receiving DC Supervisor processes inbound transfer: (i) receive against transfer order in WMS, (ii) verify quantities: compare received vs. shipped quantities, (iii) identify discrepancies: shortage (lost in transit), damage (especially for fragile items like tiles), overage (shipping DC loaded extra), (b) discrepancy resolution: (i) shortages/damage: log claim with logistics provider per W66, (ii) system posts: Dr. Inventory at Receiving DC / Cr. Inventory In-Transit, (c) putaway received items to storage locations per W3 procedures
Responsible (R): Receiving DC Supervisor / Receiving Staff
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 2–4 hours/transfer</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1423_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1423_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1423_Task11" name="Monthly transfer reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly transfer reconciliation: (a) Inventory Analyst reconciles monthly: (i) all transfer orders created vs. shipped vs. received, (ii) identify stuck transfers: shipped but not received after 14 days — investigate (lost shipment, receiving delay, system error), (iii) in-transit inventory valuation: ensure WAC is correctly applied during transfer (transferred at source DC&#x27;s WAC, not destination DC&#x27;s WAC), (iv) total inter-DC transfer volume and cost analysis (freight, handling)
Responsible (R): Inventory Analyst
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 4–6 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1423_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1423_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1423_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1423_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1423_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-254 (ensure controlled execution — Stock Transfers &amp; Rebalancing (PA-05.2).) | - operational: Supply Planning Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Supply Planning Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1423_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1423_Annotation13" targetRef="W1423_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
