    <bpmn:process id="W_W1433" name="W1433. Store-Level Daily Catch-Weight Item Inventory Valuation, WAC Calculation &amp; Shrinkage Reconciliation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily store closing (Z-report per W574); or catch-weight item sales transaction at POS per W463; or weekly cycle count including catch-weight items per W6
Frequency: Daily valuation update; weekly cycle count reconciliation for catch-weight items; monthly shrinkage analysis
Volume: ~50–100 catch-weight SKUs per store (lumber, wire, nails in bulk, pipes sold per meter); 200 stores × 50–100 SKUs = 10,000–20,000 catch-weight inventory positions
Owner: Inventory Analyst
Participants: Inventory Analyst, Store Department Supervisor, Store Manager, Finance Controller, POS System Administrator
Source: workflow W1433 — Store-Level Daily Catch-Weight Item Inventory Valuation, WAC Calculation &amp; Shrinkage Reconciliation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1433_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1433_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1433_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1433_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1433_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1433_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1433_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1433_Lane3" name="Store Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1433_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1433_Lane4" name="Inventory Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1433_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1433_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1433_Start6" name="Daily store closing (Z-report per W574); or catch-weight item sales transaction at POS…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1433_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1433_Task7" name="Daily catch-weight sales recording">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Daily catch-weight sales recording (at POS per W463): (a) when a catch-weight item is sold at POS: (i) Sales Associate weighs/measures the item (e.g., places lumber on scale, measures wire length with counter), (ii) POS captures: item code + actual weight/length, (iii) POS calculates price: actual weight/length × price per kg/m/board foot, (iv) system records: inventory reduced by actual weight/length at current WAC per unit of measure, (v) journal entry: Dr. COGS (actual weight × WAC) / Cr. Inventory (actual weight × WAC)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Cashier
Accountable (A): Store Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min/transaction</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1433_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1433_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1433_Task8" name="Daily WAC recalculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Daily WAC recalculation (at store close per W574): (a) system recalculates WAC per catch-weight SKU per store: (i) new WAC = (prior inventory value + new receipts value) ÷ (prior inventory quantity + new receipt quantity), (b) for items with new deliveries during the day: receipt weight/length must be recorded accurately at receiving per W109 — if the vendor delivers 500 kg of nails but the receiving clerk records 480 kg (scale error), the WAC calculation is distorted, (c) system posts updated WAC and inventory value per catch-weight item per store
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Inventory Analyst
Duration: Automated (&lt; 5 min/store)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1433_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1433_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1433_Task9" name="Weekly catch-weight cycle count">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Weekly catch-weight cycle count (per W6 cycle counting): (a) Store Department Supervisor conducts physical count of assigned catch-weight items: (i) lumber: count boards and measure dimensions (width × thickness × length = board feet), (ii) nails in bulk: weigh bin contents (gross weight − tare weight = net weight), (iii) wire spools: measure remaining diameter or use spool counter, (iv) pipes: count full lengths + measure cut remnants, (b) compare physical count to system quantity: (i) variance = physical quantity − system quantity, (ii) acceptable variance threshold for catch-weight items: ± 2–5% (higher than fixed-unit items due to measurement imprecision), (c) for variances exceeding threshold: investigate root cause (measurement error, customer theft, cutting waste unrecorded)
Responsible (R): Store Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–60 min/store/week (for catch-weight items only)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1433_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1433_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1433_Task10" name="Monthly shrinkage analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Monthly shrinkage analysis: (a) Inventory Analyst compiles monthly catch-weight shrinkage report: (i) total variance by category (lumber, wire, nails, pipes), (ii) variance by store (identify high-shrinkage stores), (iii) variance trend (is shrinkage increasing or decreasing?), (b) Controller reviews: (i) total catch-weight inventory shrinkage value (estimated PHP 2–5M/month chain-wide given the measurement challenges), (ii) determine if shrinkage is within acceptable range (&lt; 0.5% of catch-weight inventory value), (iii) if above threshold: escalate to Loss Prevention per W562 for investigation, (c) book inventory adjustment: Dr. Inventory Shrinkage Expense / Cr. Inventory (at WAC) for confirmed losses
Responsible (R): Inventory Analyst / Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4–6 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1433_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1433_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1433_Task11" name="Cutting waste and remnant management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Cutting waste and remnant management: (a) when a catch-weight item is cut for a customer (e.g., 10-foot pipe cut to 6 feet, leaving 4-foot remnant): (i) Sales Associate records: item code, original length, cut length, remnant length, (ii) system adjusts: original piece derecognized, sold piece recognized at WAC × sold length, remnant recognized at WAC × remnant length (if remnant is resalable — above minimum saleable length), (iii) if remnant is below minimum saleable length (scrap): recognized at zero value → Dr. Cutting Waste Expense / Cr. Inventory, (b) Store Department Supervisor monitors remnant accumulation: excessive remnants indicate cutting waste that could be reduced with better measurement
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Store Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–3 min/cut</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1433_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1433_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1433_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1433_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1433_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-254 (ensure controlled execution — Stock Transfers &amp; Rebalancing (PA-05.2).) | - operational: Inventory Analyst review and approval gate
Owner: Inventory Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1433_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1433_Annotation13" targetRef="W1433_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1433_Flow15" sourceRef="W1433_Start6" targetRef="W1433_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1433_Flow16" sourceRef="W1433_Task7" targetRef="W1433_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1433_Flow17" sourceRef="W1433_Task8" targetRef="W1433_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1433_Flow18" sourceRef="W1433_Task9" targetRef="W1433_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1433_Flow19" sourceRef="W1433_Task10" targetRef="W1433_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1433_Flow20" sourceRef="W1433_Task11" targetRef="W1433_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1433_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1433_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1433">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1433_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1433_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1433_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1433_Lane4_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Lane4" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="590" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1433_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1433_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1433_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1433_Task10_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Task10"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="635" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1433_Task11_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Task11"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1433_Start6_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Start6"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1433_End12_di" bpmnElement="W1433_End12"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="657" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1433_Annotation13_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Annotation13"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="800" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1433_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1433_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1433_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1433_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="675" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1433_Flow19_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Flow19"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="675" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1433_Flow20_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Flow20"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="1470" y="675" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1433_Assoc14_di" bpmnElement="W1433_Assoc14"><di:waypoint x="340" y="800" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1535" name="W1535. Emergency Inter-DC Stock Transfer for Critical Out-of-Stock Prevention" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Category A-item stockout at a DC serving ≥ 5 stores with no incoming PO within lead time; or store-level stockout of promotional item with active marketing spend
Frequency: ~8–12 emergency transfers/month across all DC pairs
Volume: Typically 5–20 SKUs per emergency transfer; high-value or high-velocity items
Owner: Supply Planning Manager
Participants: Supply Planning Manager, DC Managers (source &amp; destination), Logistics Planner, Category Manager
Source: workflow W1535 — Emergency Inter-DC Stock Transfer for Critical Out-of-Stock Prevention</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1535_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1535_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1535_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1535_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1535_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1535_Lane2" name="Supply Planning Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1535_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1535_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1535_Lane3" name="DC Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1535_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1535_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1535_Lane4" name="Supply Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1535_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1535_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1535_Start6" name="Category A-item stockout at a DC serving ≥ 5 stores with no incoming PO within lead time…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1535_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1535_Task7" name="Stockout alert &amp; assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Stockout alert &amp; assessment: System flags critical stockout — A-item at zero available quantity at DC with ≥ 5 stores showing negative ATP in next 7 days; Supply Planning Manager reviews: (a) Is there an incoming PO within lead time? (b) Can DSD vendors supply directly? (c) Is the stockout store-cluster specific or region-wide?
Responsible (R): System / Supply Planning Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1535_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1535_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1535_Task8" name="Surplus DC identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Surplus DC identification: System queries all other DCs for available quantity of the affected SKU(s); ranks by: (a) surplus days-of-supply (&gt; 21 days preferred), (b) shipping distance/transit time to affected DC, (c) inter-island route availability
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1535_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1535_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1535_Task9" name="Emergency transfer authorization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Emergency transfer authorization: If transfer is warranted (revenue at risk &gt; PHP 500K or promotional commitment affected), Supply Planning Manager creates emergency transfer order; VP Supply Chain approves if total transfer value &gt; PHP 200K or requires air freight
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1535_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1535_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1535_Task10" name="Expedited pick &amp; ship">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Expedited pick &amp; ship: Source DC receives priority pick directive — emergency transfer order jumps queue ahead of standard replenishment orders; Logistics Planner books fastest available inter-island transport (RoRo ferry, fast craft, or for extreme urgency air freight via W1514)
Responsible (R): DC Supervisor / Logistics Planner
Accountable (A): DC Manager (source)
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1535_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1535_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1535_Task11" name="In-transit tracking &amp; store allocation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: In-transit tracking &amp; store allocation: System tracks emergency shipment with heightened monitoring; destination DC pre-allocates incoming stock to highest-priority store replenishment orders; Category Manager may adjust promotional allocation based on incoming emergency quantity
Responsible (R): Supply Planner
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1535_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1535_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1535_Task12" name="Receipt &amp; rush distribution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Receipt &amp; rush distribution: Destination DC receives emergency shipment; priority putaway directly to forward-pick locations (bypass standard putaway); immediate release to outbound delivery wave for affected stores
Responsible (R): DC Supervisor (destination)
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1535_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1535_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1535_Task13" name="Post-event review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-event review: Supply Planning Manager conducts root cause analysis — why did the stockout occur? (forecast miss, vendor delay, demand surge?); feeds into S&amp;OP process (W1533) to prevent recurrence; documents emergency transfer cost (expedited shipping premium) for category P&amp;L impact
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1 hour/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1535_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1535_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1535_End14" name="Complete">
